":"Flash Flood Warning","headline":"Flash Flood Warning issued August 15 at 3:36PM MDT until August 15 at 5:45PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"At 336 PM MDT, Broadcast media reported flash flooding was occurring\nnear Chambers and Iliff, and Mississippi and Havana. Between 1.5 and\n3 inches of rain have fallen. Additional rainfall amounts up to 0.2\ninches are possible in the warned area. Flash flooding is already\noccurring.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Heavy rain producing flash\nflooding.\n\nSOURCE...Broadcast media reported.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams,\nroads, and low lying areas.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nEastern Denver, Aurora, and Buckley SFB.\n\nThis includes the following streams and drainages...\nToll Gate Creek, Sand Creek, Cherry Creek, South Platte River,\nFirst Creek, East Toll Gate Creek, West Toll Gate Creek, Murphy\nCreek, Coal Creek, Westerly Creek, Third Creek and Second Creek.","ends":"2026-08-15T17:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Adams, CO; Western Arapahoe, CO; Denver, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0a3442297a267fb83636a62cc0b9d378cc47647b.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0a3442297a267fb83636a62cc0b9d378cc47647b.001.1"},{"event":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch","headline":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch issued August 15 at 2:05PM MDT until August 15 at 9:00PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"THE NATIONAL WEATHER SERVICE HAS ISSUED SEVERE THUNDERSTORM WATCH\n584 IN EFFECT UNTIL 9 PM MDT THIS EVENING FOR THE FOLLOWING AREAS\n\nIN COLORADO THIS WATCH INCLUDES 9 COUNTIES\n\nIN EAST CENTRAL COLORADO\n\nELBERT                LINCOLN\n\nIN NORTHEAST COLORADO\n\nADAMS                 ARAPAHOE              DOUGLAS\nLOGAN                 MORGAN                WASHINGTON\nWELD\n\nTHIS INCLUDES THE CITIES OF AKRON, AURORA, CASTLE ROCK,\nCENTENNIAL, ELIZABETH, FORT MORGAN, GREELEY, KIOWA, LIMON,\nPARKER, STERLING, THORNTON, WESTMINSTER, AND WINDSOR.","ends":"2026-08-15T21:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Adams, CO; Arapahoe, CO; Douglas, CO; Elbert, CO; Lincoln, CO; Logan, CO; Morgan, CO; Washington, CO; Weld, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.862838f8b61c9032ddaddac2ecfc011791cca58a.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.862838f8b61c9032ddaddac2ecfc011791cca58a.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Advisory","headline":"Flood Advisory issued August 15 at 12:09PM MDT until August 15 at 9:00PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding along Bijou Creek caused by excessive rainfall.\n\n* WHERE...Rural and low lying areas along Bijou Creek in northern\nElbert, Central Adams, Central Arapahoe, and southwestern Morgan\nCounties.\n\n* WHEN...Until 900 PM MDT Saturday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding along Bijou Creek.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 1204 PM MDT, Local law enforcement reported flooding had\noccurred along Bijou Creek through Adams County. Water had caused\ncloser of a couple county roads, but they have since reopened.\nWater had also crested and spilled onto Colfax Avenue in rural\nAdams County. The crest has passed this area, but will continue\nmoving downstream and affect areas farther north through the Hoyt\narea and toward the confluence with the South Platte River in\nMorgan County.\n\n- This includes the following streams and drainages...\nWest Bijou Creek and Bijou Creek.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nrural and low lying areas along Bijou Creek.","ends":"2026-08-15T21:00:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Adams, CO; Arapahoe, CO; Elbert, CO; Morgan, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1646ae29d946a597182721f07707f12e6538bdc8.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1646ae29d946a597182721f07707f12e6538bdc8.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued August 15 at 11:52AM MDT until August 15 at 10:00PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flash Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of central and northeast Colorado, including the\nfollowing areas: the southern Front Range Foothills, Palmer Divide\narea, I-25 corridor, and all of our eastern plains counties.\n\n* WHEN...Until 10 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nFlooding may occur in poor drainage and urban areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Additional thunderstorms and heavy rainfall this afternoon,\ncombined with the heavy rainfall from the past 3 days, will bring\na threat for flash flooding this afternoon and evening. Stronger\nstorms will be capable of producing 1 to 2 inches of rain in 30\nminutes, with isolated areas receiving storm totals of 2 to 4\ninches.","ends":"2026-08-15T22:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Jefferson and West Douglas Counties Above  6000 Feet/Gilpin/Clear Creek/Northeast Park Counties Below 9000 Feet; Larimer County Below 6000 Feet/Northwest Weld County; Boulder And Jefferson Counties Below 6000 Feet/West Broomfield County; North Douglas County Below 6000 Feet/Denver/West Adams and Arapahoe Counties/East Broomfield County; Elbert/Central and East Douglas Counties Above 6000 Feet; Northeast Weld County; Central and South Weld County; Morgan County; Central and East Adams and Arapahoe Counties; North and Northeast Elbert County Below 6000 Feet/North Lincoln County; Southeast Elbert County Below 6000 Feet/South Lincoln County; Logan County; Washington County; Sedgwick County; Phillips County","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.eea7fe66bbe726127cab571e453d260029b0d72c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.eea7fe66bbe726127cab571e453d260029b0d72c.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-15T19:12:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 151912 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 112 PM MDT Sat Aug 